        <body>
            <div xml:id="d956">

                <pb facs="0755" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8259</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Blocker to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eagle Pass, Texas</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-06T22:00:00-06:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 6, 1916, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>An American citizen, by name L. Naudin, arrived Eagle Pass this evening from
                    Parral having left there four days ago after being prisoner of Villistas, but
                    secured his liberty on plea of being a French subject. Conferred with him and
                    learned following:</p>
                <p>All of the Americans left there before Villistas entered with exception of 6, by
                    name Jake Myer, Walter C. Palmer, Dr. Flannigan, William Scott, Howard Gray and
                    L. Naudin himself who found hiding places among Mexican friends, and until the
                    second day after Villistas had entered all went well, but upon second day Gray
                    and himself were found and immediately ordered to be shot on grounds they were
                    American citizens. Gray met his fate and now lies unburied in Parral while
                    Naudin secured release on grounds stated above. The remaining 4 Americans are
                    still hid and have so far not been detected; however, grave fear is felt for
                    their safety.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blocker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
